    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d597">

                <pb facs="1430" n="1414" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/9–2551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">GATT</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d597-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-25T19:00:00-04:00">September 25,
                            1951—7 p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Gatt 39. For Thorp. Today Secy spoke Gasperi<anchor n="2" xml:id="d597-f2"/> re
                    GATT vote on Czech issue. Gasperi promised consider carefully but stated he
                    uninformed. Suggest you inform Ital deleg and request he inquire for affirmative
                    decision.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d597-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d597-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Rome as 1394.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d597-f2" n="2" xml:id="d597-f2-content">
                <p>Italian Prime Minister Alcide De Gasperi was engaged in talks with the United
                    States Government at this time in Washington, following a session of the North
                    Atlantic Council in Ottawa, Canada; for documentation on these meetings, see
                        <ref target="frus1951v04p1">volume IV</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
